🔐 What Are Network Policies in EKS?

Network Policies in Kubernetes allow you to control Pod-to-Pod and Pod-to-external traffic using Layer 3/4 firewall rules.

By default, in EKS (and all Kubernetes):

❗ EVERYTHING can talk to EVERYTHING

Unless you apply a Network Policy.

Network Policies let you restrict:

Which Pods can talk to other Pods

Which Namespaces can talk to others

Which IPs / CIDRs can access Pods

Which Ports are allowed

1️⃣ Deny All Traffic to a Namespace (Zero Trust mode)

By default Kubernetes allows all traffic.
To start applying restrictive rules, first DENY all:

apiVersion: networking.k8s.io/v1
kind: NetworkPolicy
metadata:
  name: deny-all
  namespace: dev
spec:
  podSelector: {}
  policyTypes:
    - Ingress
    - Egress

=======================================
2️⃣ Allow only specific Pods to talk to a service

Example: Only Pods with label role=frontend can talk to role=backend service.

apiVersion: networking.k8s.io/v1
kind: NetworkPolicy
metadata:
  name: allow-frontend-to-backend
  namespace: dev
spec:
  podSelector:
    matchLabels:
      role: backend
  ingress:
    - from:
        - podSelector:
            matchLabels:
              role: frontend
      ports:
        - protocol: TCP
          port: 8080


===========================================================

3️⃣ Allow only traffic from a specific Namespace
apiVersion: networking.k8s.io/v1
kind: NetworkPolicy
metadata:
  name: allow-namespace-dev
spec:
  podSelector:
    matchLabels:
      role: api
  ingress:
    - from:
        - namespaceSelector:
            matchLabels:
              env: dev


==============================================================

4️⃣ Allow egress only to a specific external IP range (e.g., DB subnet)
apiVersion: networking.k8s.io/v1
kind: NetworkPolicy
metadata:
  name: allow-egress-to-rds
spec:
  podSelector:
    matchLabels:
      app: backend
  policyTypes:
    - Egress
  egress:
    - to:
        - ipBlock:
            cidr: 10.10.2.0/24   # RDS subnet
      ports:
        - protocol: TCP
          port: 5432


Pods cannot access internet or any other service unless allowed.
